A tourism board’s media release is headed "**Visitor numbers rise every month in record boom**" and attaches the figures below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.62]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,9.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(15.5,0);
\foreach \y in {20,40,60,80} {\draw (-0.2,\y/10)--(0,\y/10); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y/10) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw (0.8,0) rectangle (2.3,4.2);
\draw (3.1,0) rectangle (4.6,5.5);
\draw (5.4,0) rectangle (6.9,4.8);
\draw (7.7,0) rectangle (9.2,6.1);
\draw (10.0,0) rectangle (11.5,5.8);
\draw (12.3,0) rectangle (13.8,6.6);
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1.55,0) {Jan};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3.85,0) {Feb};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (6.15,0) {Mar};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (8.45,0) {Apr};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (10.75,0) {May};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (13.05,0) {Jun};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,4) {Visitors (1000s)};
\node[below] at (7.55,-1.0) {Month};
\node at (7.55,9.1) {Visitors each month};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which statement about the release is correct?
